      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given:  \n$(2\\left(3\\right)+5)^{2}=4^{2}=4\\times 4 = 16$.\n\nTo determine the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we start by substituting \\(x = 3\\) into the expression. This gives us:\n\n\\[\n(2(3) + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the multiplication inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2(3) = 6\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n(6 + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the numbers inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n6 + 5 = 11\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n11^2\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(11^2\\):\n\n\\[\n11^2 = 11 \\times 11\n\\]\n\nWe know that:\n\n\\[\n11 \\times 11 = 121\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{121}\n\\]",
